class.description:
[UZUSfx] makes short game sounds (hits, jumps, pickups, explosions) in the style of the sfxr family of tools. A sound is a waveform whose pitch slides and jumps, shaped by an envelope and an optional low-pass filter. The result is a 16-bit mono [AudioStreamWAV].
A table of presets gives starting points, and a seed varies them a little. [method play] plays a sound once, with a small random change of pitch and volume, so repeated sounds do not feel mechanical. [method describe] reports what a sound is like (length, peak, loudness, pitch at the start and the end), for an agent that cannot listen.
[codeblock]
var coin = UZUSfx.generate_preset("coin", 3)
UZUSfx.play(self, coin)
var params = UZUSfx.get_preset("laser")
params["decay"] = 0.4
var longer_laser = UZUSfx.generate(params)
[/codeblock]
[b]Note:[/b] This class is specific to U.ZU Engine (UZUJuice).
